.TH stralloc_nul 3
.SH NAME
stralloc_nul \- append a null byte to a stralloc
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <stralloc.h>

int stralloc_nul(stralloc *\fIsa\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stralloc_nul
ensures there is enough space in the
.I stralloc
structure pointed to by
.I sa
to append a null byte ('\0'), and then appends it.
.PP
Unlike
.B stralloc_append
or
.B stralloc_cat,
this function does not increment the
.I sa->len
member; it only ensures the byte at
.I sa->s[sa->len]
is set to null. This is useful for null-terminating a string buffer managed by a
.I stralloc
without modifying its recorded length.
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 if the operation was successful, 0 if it failed (e.g., due to memory allocation failure).
.SH SEE ALSO
stralloc_readyplus(3), stralloc_append(3)